lf", "firstName": "William", "initials": "W", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular and Clinical Cancer Medicine, Institute of Translational Medicine, University of Liverpool, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Jeon CY", "lastName": "Jeon", "firstName": "Christie Y", "initials": "CY", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Medicine, Division of Digestive and Liver Diseases, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Koay EJ", "lastName": "Koay", "firstName": "Eugene J", "initials": "EJ", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center, Houston, TX, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Almario CV", "lastName": "Almario", "firstName": "Christopher V", "initials": "CV", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0664-9479"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Medicine, Division of Digestive and Liver Diseases, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, CA, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Halloran C", "lastName": "Halloran", "firstName": "Christopher", "initials": "C", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5471-4178"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular and Clinical Cancer Medicine, Institute of Translational Medicine, University of Liverpool, UK."}]}}, {"fullName": "Lennon AM", "lastName": "Lennon", "firstName": "Anne Marie", "initials": "AM", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Division of Gastroenterology and Hepatology, Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Costello E", "lastName": "Costello", "firstName": "Eithne", "initials": "E", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Molecular and Clinical Cancer Medicine, Institute of Translational Medicine, University of Liverpool, UK. Electronic address: ecostell@liverpool.ac.uk."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7477-4541"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-8560-8231"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0839-402X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5471-4178"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0664-9479"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0821-1809"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "7", "volume": "5", "journalIssueId": 2968941, "dateOfPublication": "2020 Jul", "monthOfPublication": 7, "yearOfPublication": 2020, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Lancet Gastroenterol Hepatol", "title": "The lancet. Gastroenterology & hepatology", "essn": "2468-1253", "issn": "2468-1253", "nlmid": "101690683", "isoabbreviation": "Lancet Gastroenterol Hepatol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2020-07-01"}, "pubYear": "2020", "pageInfo": "698-710", "abstractText": "Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma is most frequently detected at an advanced stage. Such late detection restricts treatment options and contributes to a dismal 5-year survival rate of 3-15%. Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma is relatively uncommon and screening of the asymptomatic adult population is not feasible or recommended with current modalities. However, screening of individuals in high-risk groups is recommended. Here, we review groups at high risk for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma, including individuals with inherited predisposition and patients with pancreatic cystic lesions. We discuss studies aimed at finding ways of identifying pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma in high-risk groups, such as among individuals with new-onset diabetes mellitus and people attending primary and secondary care practices with symptoms that suggest this cancer. We review early detection biomarkers, explore the potential of using social media for detection, appraise prediction models developed using electronic health records and research data, and examine the application of artificial intelligence to medical imaging for the purposes of early detection.", "affiliation": "Institute for Liver and Digestive Health, University College London, London, UK.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA230442", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences", "grantId": "U01CA196403–01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Pancreas Foundation", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Pancreatic Cancer Action Network", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "P50 CA062924", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "R01 CA218004", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Pancreatic Cancer UK", "acronym": "PANCREATICCANUK_", "grantId": "RG2014_01_Pereria", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases", "grantId": "U01DK108314", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences", "grantId": "UL1TR001881–01", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases", "grantId": "R01CA230442", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantId": "U01 DK108327", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Pancreatic Cancer Research Fund", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Royal College of Surgeons of Edinburgh", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Cancer Research UK", "acronym": "CRUK_", "grantId": "C52547/A28210", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institute for Health Research (NIHR)", "acronym": "DH_", "grantId": "PB-PG-0712-28114", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CA", "grantId": "U01 CA200468", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantI